</table>
</div>
<div id="S11.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p5.1" class="ltx_p">“Bulk” is the middle half of the nodes; the loss of accuracy near
<math id="S11.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S11.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=n</annotation></semantics></math> is the known endpoint effect, where an expansion of
Bessel type must be used instead.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Computational checks</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The identities of this paper have been checked independently by exact
computation in finite ranges, in rational, Gaussian-rational or symbolic
arithmetic. In particular, the numbers <math id="Sx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> were computed for
<math id="Sx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 41</annotation></semantics></math> directly from the amplitude (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), and they agree with
(<a href="#S1.E13" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) (real and imaginary parts) and with
(<a href="#S10.E98" title="In 10. The tangent from the layers, and four valuation formulas ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">98</span></a>); the relation (<a href="#S7.E88" title="In Theorem 7.34. ‣ 7.7. The arithmetic step: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">88</span></a>) was checked
against these values for <math id="Sx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq 19" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq 19</annotation></semantics></math>; the valuation formula
(<a href="#S7.E87" title="In Theorem 7.33. ‣ 7.7. The arithmetic step: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>) was checked for <math id="Sx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq 159" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>159</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq 159</annotation></semantics></math>; and the valuation
formulas of Section <a href="#S10" title="10. The tangent from the layers, and four valuation formulas ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> were checked for <math id="Sx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq 21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq 21</annotation></semantics></math>.
The identities of Section <a href="#S7" title="7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and
Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> that involve boundary values, lattice sums
and their asymptotic expansions were checked numerically to at least
<math id="Sx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math> digits. None of these computations is used in the proofs, with
the exception of the finite verification in
Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem37" title="Proposition 7.37. ‣ 7.7. The arithmetic step: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.37</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>The sectorial estimates</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix proves the estimates stated in Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem27" title="Lemma 7.27. ‣ 7.6. The asymptotic matching: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.27</span></a>,
the vanishing of the constant <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{*}(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{*}(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> of the quadrature
(<a href="#S7.E48" title="In item (ii) ‣ Theorem 7.9. ‣ 7.2. The boundary split and the transverse quadrature ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) on every admissible lattice
(Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem12" title="Theorem A.12. ‣ A.5. The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice constant ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>), and Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a>. The order
is as follows: coefficient bounds and the expansion of the amplitude in
a bilateral sector (Subsection <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>); uniform
asymptotics of the closed blocks (Subsection <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>); the
uniform expansion of the forcing <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and of its
lattice sum <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (Subsection <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>); the relation
between the two boundary determinations, from which the vertical decay
of the quotient <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> follows (Subsection <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4. The two-component relation and vertical decay ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>); a
classification lemma for periodic meromorphic functions and the
vanishing of <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{*}(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{*}(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> (Subsection <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5. The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice constant ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>); and the proof
of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a> (Subsection <a href="#A1.SS6" title="A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>). The
only classical inputs are Stirling’s formula in sectors, the
Euler–Maclaurin (Hurwitz) expansion, and the removability of bounded
isolated singularities.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1. </span>Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=1-2s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=1-2s</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\alpha;Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\alpha;Z)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the
specialisation <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math> of the amplitude (<a href="#S1.E6" title="In 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\alpha;Z)=\sum_{n\geq 0}G_{n}(\alpha)\,e_{n}(Z),\qquad e_{n}(Z)=\frac{1}{(Z-1)\cdots(Z-n)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\alpha;Z)=\sum_{n\geq 0}G_{n}(\alpha)\,e_{n}(Z),\qquad e_{n}(Z)=\frac{1}{(Z-1)\cdots(Z-n)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{n}(\alpha)=\sum_{l=0}^{n}a_{l}(\alpha)\,a_{n-l}(0)\,p^{l}q^{\,n-l}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{n}(\alpha)=\sum_{l=0}^{n}a_{l}(\alpha)\,a_{n-l}(0)\,p^{l}q^{\,n-l},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=1+i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=1+i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=1-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=1-i</annotation></semantics></math> and the Hankel coefficients <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of
the Introduction. Two facts proved in the main text are used. First, by
Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a> the series <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is the Kampé de Fériet double
series (<a href="#S7.E36" title="In Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) at the midpoint arguments
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{0},y_{0})=(\frac{1+i}{2},\frac{1-i}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{0},y_{0})=(\frac{1+i}{2},\frac{1-i}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, grouped by total degree
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu+\nu=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu+\nu=n</annotation></semantics></math>. Second, by (<a href="#S7.E38" title="In Branch convention. ‣ 7.1. The Appell 𝐹_3 specialization on the physical curve ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) (an exact identity for
fixed <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>),</p>
<table id="A1.E100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(100)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\alpha;Z)=y_{0}^{-Z}(-i)^{1/2}\,\mathcal{H}(\alpha;Z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\alpha;Z)=y_{0}^{-Z}(-i)^{1/2}\,\mathcal{H}(\alpha;Z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with an <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-independent prefactor, so that</p>
<table id="A1.E101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(101)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(s)=\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{\partial_{\alpha}^{2}\mathcal{H}(0;Z)}{\mathcal{H}(0;Z)}=\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{\partial_{\alpha}^{2}F(0;Z)}{F(0;Z)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(s)=\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{\partial_{\alpha}^{2}\mathcal{H}(0;Z)}{\mathcal{H}(0;Z)}=\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{\partial_{\alpha}^{2}F(0;Z)}{F(0;Z)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">as an identity of functions, not merely of formal series.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|a_{k}(\alpha)|\leq\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)\,k!\,2^{-k},\qquad\text{and consequently}\qquad|G_{n}(\alpha)|\leq\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)\,(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>cosh</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and consequently</mtext><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>cosh</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{k}(\alpha)|\leq\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)\,k!\,2^{-k},\qquad\text{and consequently}\qquad|G_{n}(\alpha)|\leq\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)\,(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the product form
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}(\nu)=\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}\bigl(4\nu^{2}-(2j+1)^{2}\bigr)/(8^{k}k!)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}(\nu)=\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}\bigl(4\nu^{2}-(2j+1)^{2}\bigr)/(8^{k}k!)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{k}(\alpha)|\leq|a_{k}(0)|\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}\Bigl(1+\frac{4|\alpha|^{2}}{(2j+1)^{2}}\Bigr)\leq|a_{k}(0)|\prod_{j\geq 0}\Bigl(1+\frac{4|\alpha|^{2}}{(2j+1)^{2}}\Bigr)=|a_{k}(0)|\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cosh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{k}(\alpha)|\leq|a_{k}(0)|\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}\Bigl(1+\frac{4|\alpha|^{2}}{(2j+1)^{2}}\Bigr)\leq|a_{k}(0)|\prod_{j\geq 0}\Bigl(1+\frac{4|\alpha|^{2}}{(2j+1)^{2}}\Bigr)=|a_{k}(0)|\cosh(\pi|\alpha|),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">the last step being the product formula
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos(\pi z/2)=\prod_{j\geq 0}(1-z^{2}/(2j+1)^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos(\pi z/2)=\prod_{j\geq 0}(1-z^{2}/(2j+1)^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=2i|\alpha|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=2i|\alpha|</annotation></semantics></math>. For
the central value, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{k}(0)|=\bigl((2k-1)!!\bigr)^{2}/(8^{k}k!)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!!</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{k}(0)|=\bigl((2k-1)!!\bigr)^{2}/(8^{k}k!)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl((2k-1)!!\bigr)^{2}\leq(2k-1)!!\,(2k)!!=(2k)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!!</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!!</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl((2k-1)!!\bigr)^{2}\leq(2k-1)!!\,(2k)!!=(2k)!</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{k}(0)|\leq(2k)!/(8^{k}k!)=k!\binom{2k}{k}8^{-k}\leq k!\,4^{k}/8^{k}=k!\,2^{-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>8</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn> 4</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{k}(0)|\leq(2k)!/(8^{k}k!)=k!\binom{2k}{k}8^{-k}\leq k!\,4^{k}/8^{k}=k!\,2^{-k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p|=|q|=\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p|=|q|=\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l=0}^{n}l!\,(n-l)!\leq(n+1)\,n!=(n+1)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l=0}^{n}l!\,(n-l)!\leq(n+1)\,n!=(n+1)!</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|G_{n}(\alpha)|\leq\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)\,2^{n/2}\,2^{-n}\,(n+1)!=\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>cosh</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>cosh</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|G_{n}(\alpha)|\leq\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)\,2^{n/2}\,2^{-n}\,(n+1)!=\cosh(\pi|\alpha|)(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\theta_{0}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\theta_{0}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\min}\geq 1/(1-\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\min}\geq 1/(1-\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> put</p>
<table id="A1.E102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(102)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E102.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Omega_{\theta_{0}}:=\bigl\{Z:\ |\operatorname{Re}Z|\leq\theta_{0}\,|\operatorname{Im}Z|,\ |\operatorname{Im}Z|\geq y_{\min}\bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.500em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Re</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Im</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Im</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\theta_{0}}:=\bigl\{Z:\ |\operatorname{Re}Z|\leq\theta_{0}\,|\operatorname{Im}Z|,\ |\operatorname{Im}Z|\geq y_{\min}\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Both signs of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}Z</annotation></semantics></math> are allowed: the region is symmetric
under conjugation, and every vertical strip
<math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Re}Z|\leq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Re}Z|\leq h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}Z|\geq h/\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}Z|\geq h/\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
lies inside it.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\Omega_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\Omega_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j+1)\leq\sqrt{2}\,|Z-j|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j+1)\leq\sqrt{2}\,|Z-j|</annotation></semantics></math> for
every integer <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau_{M}(Z):=\sum_{n\geq M+1}(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}\prod_{j=M+1}^{n}|Z-j|^{-1}\ \leq\ (M+1)!\,2^{-M/2}\,\bigl(18|Z|+4\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>18</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{M}(Z):=\sum_{n\geq M+1}(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}\prod_{j=M+1}^{n}|Z-j|^{-1}\ \leq\ (M+1)!\,2^{-M/2}\,\bigl(18|Z|+4\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\operatorname{Re}Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\operatorname{Re}Z</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=|\operatorname{Im}Z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=|\operatorname{Im}Z|</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a|\leq\theta_{0}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a|\leq\theta_{0}b</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq 1/(1-\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq 1/(1-\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}b+1\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}b+1\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2|Z-j|^{2}-(j+1)^{2}=2(j-a)^{2}+2b^{2}-(j+1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2|Z-j|^{2}-(j+1)^{2}=2(j-a)^{2}+2b^{2}-(j+1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; as a function of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> this
quadratic has positive leading coefficient and minimum value
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2b^{2}-2(a+1)^{2}\geq 2b^{2}-2(\theta_{0}b+1)^{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2b^{2}-2(a+1)^{2}\geq 2b^{2}-2(\theta_{0}b+1)^{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which proves
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j+1)\leq\sqrt{2}|Z-j|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j+1)\leq\sqrt{2}|Z-j|</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently the terms
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{n}:=(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}\prod_{j=M+1}^{n}|Z-j|^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}:=(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}\prod_{j=M+1}^{n}|Z-j|^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}/t_{n-1}=(n+1)/(\sqrt{2}\,|Z-n|)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}/t_{n-1}=(n+1)/(\sqrt{2}\,|Z-n|)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{n}\leq t_{M}=(M+1)!\,2^{-M/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}\leq t_{M}=(M+1)!\,2^{-M/2}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;M</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover for
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 18|Z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 18|Z|</annotation></semantics></math> one has <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z-n|\geq n-|Z|\geq n(1-\tfrac{1}{18})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z-n|\geq n-|Z|\geq n(1-\tfrac{1}{18})</annotation></semantics></math> and hence
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}/t_{n-1}\leq\frac{18\,(n+1)}{17\sqrt{2}\,n}\leq\frac{4}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}/t_{n-1}\leq\frac{18\,(n+1)}{17\sqrt{2}\,n}\leq\frac{4}{5}</annotation></semantics></math> once
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 18|Z|\geq 18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 18|Z|\geq 18</annotation></semantics></math>. Splitting the sum at <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18|Z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18|Z|</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{M}\leq t_{M}\bigl(18|Z|\bigr)+t_{M}\sum_{r\geq 1}(4/5)^{r}\leq t_{M}(18|Z|+4).\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{M}\leq t_{M}\bigl(18|Z|\bigr)+t_{M}\sum_{r\geq 1}(4/5)^{r}\leq t_{M}(18|Z|+4).\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\theta_{0}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\theta_{0}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the double series (</span><a href="#S7.E36" title="In Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) converges
absolutely for every </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\notin\{1,2,3,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\notin\{1,2,3,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and every </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; its
grouping by </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu+\nu=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu+\nu=n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the series </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\alpha;Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\alpha;Z)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> above, which is
therefore analytic in </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,Z)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on
</span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}\times(\mathbb{C}\setminus\{1,2,\dots\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}\times(\mathbb{C}\setminus\{1,2,\dots\})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and satisfies
(</span><a href="#A1.E100" title="In A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">100</span></a><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) there;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for every </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> there are </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{N}=C_{N}(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{N}=C_{N}(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and
</span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\min}=y_{\min}(\theta_{0},N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\min}=y_{\min}(\theta_{0},N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that, uniformly for </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\Omega_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\Omega_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and
</span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|F(\alpha;Z)-\sum_{m=0}^{N}c_{m}(\alpha)Z^{-m}\Bigr|\leq C_{N}\,|Z|^{-N-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|F(\alpha;Z)-\sum_{m=0}^{N}c_{m}(\alpha)Z^{-m}\Bigr|\leq C_{N}\,|Z|^{-N-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{m}(\alpha)=\sum_{n\leq m}G_{n}(\alpha)\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{m}(\alpha)=\sum_{n\leq m}G_{n}(\alpha)\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are the plain
coefficients of Lemma </span><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3. From half-integers to all 𝛼 ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; the same bound holds for
</span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\alpha}^{k}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\alpha}^{k}F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\alpha}^{k}c_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\alpha}^{k}c_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">consequently, uniformly for </span><math id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\Omega_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\Omega_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
(</span><em id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph">both</em><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> signs of </span><math id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}Z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">),</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|\mathcal{A}(s)-\sum_{n=1}^{N}g_{n}Z^{-n}\Bigr|\leq C_{N}^{\prime}\,|Z|^{-N-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|\mathcal{A}(s)-\sum_{n=1}^{N}g_{n}Z^{-n}\Bigr|\leq C_{N}^{\prime}\,|Z|^{-N-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">(i) With <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|x_{0}|=|y_{0}|=2^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x_{0}|=|y_{0}|=2^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the modulus of the
<math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math>-term of (<a href="#S7.E36" title="In Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) is at most
<math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C(\alpha)\,\frac{\mu!\,\nu!}{|(1-Z)_{\mu+\nu}|}\,2^{-(\mu+\nu)/2}\mu^{O(1)}\nu^{O(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\alpha)\,\frac{\mu!\,\nu!}{|(1-Z)_{\mu+\nu}|}\,2^{-(\mu+\nu)/2}\mu^{O(1)}\nu^{O(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> applied to each
Pochhammer pair, and
<math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu!\,\nu!/(\mu+\nu)!=\binom{\mu+\nu}{\mu}^{-1}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu!\,\nu!/(\mu+\nu)!=\binom{\mu+\nu}{\mu}^{-1}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> while
<math id="A1.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(1-Z)_{m}|\geq c(Z)\,m!\,m^{-\operatorname{Re}Z-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(1-Z)_{m}|\geq c(Z)\,m!\,m^{-\operatorname{Re}Z-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> large, by
Stirling; the sum over <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu+\nu=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu+\nu=m</annotation></semantics></math> then converges geometrically in
<math id="A1.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Grouping the absolutely convergent double series by <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu+\nu=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu+\nu=n</annotation></semantics></math>
gives <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}e_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}e_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly as in the proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 7.2. ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>.
Identity (<a href="#A1.E100" title="In A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">100</span></a>) holds for each fixed generic <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> by
Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 7.3. ‣ Branch convention. ‣ 7.1. The Appell 𝐹_3 specialization on the physical curve ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a> and (<a href="#S7.E38" title="In Branch convention. ‣ 7.1. The Appell 𝐹_3 specialization on the physical curve ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>), and both
sides are analytic off the indicated sets, so it holds on the whole
common domain.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(ii) Split <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sum_{n\leq N}G_{n}e_{n}+\mathrm{Rem}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Rem</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sum_{n\leq N}G_{n}e_{n}+\mathrm{Rem}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, is
analytic at <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{n}=\sum_{m=n}^{N}\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}Z^{-m}+O_{N}(|Z|^{-N-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mfrac linethickness="0.0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{n}=\sum_{m=n}^{N}\genfrac{}{}{0.0pt}{}{m}{n}Z^{-m}+O_{N}(|Z|^{-N-1})</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly for
<math id="A1.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z|\geq 2N+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z|\geq 2N+2</annotation></semantics></math> (finitely many geometric expansions of
<math id="A1.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{-n}\prod_{j\leq n}(1-j/Z)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{-n}\prod_{j\leq n}(1-j/Z)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>), which produces the polynomial part
<math id="A1.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m\leq N}c_{m}Z^{-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m\leq N}c_{m}Z^{-m}</annotation></semantics></math> with the stated coefficients plus an error
<math id="A1.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{N}(|Z|^{-N-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{N}(|Z|^{-N-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. For the tail, reserve the first <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+2</annotation></semantics></math> factors:
for <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq N+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq N+2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j=1}^{n}|Z-j|\ \geq\ |\operatorname{Im}Z|^{\,N+2}\prod_{j=N+3}^{n}|Z-j|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j=1}^{n}|Z-j|\ \geq\ |\operatorname{Im}Z|^{\,N+2}\prod_{j=N+3}^{n}|Z-j|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">so by Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> (with <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=N+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=N+2</annotation></semantics></math>),</span></p>
<table id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathrm{Rem}_{N}|\leq\sum_{n=N+1}^{N+2}\frac{|G_{n}|}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{\,n}}+\frac{\cosh\pi}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{N+2}}\,\tau_{N+2}(Z)\\
\leq\frac{C_{N}^{\prime\prime}}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{N+1}}+\frac{C_{N}^{\prime\prime\prime}\,|Z|}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{N+2}}\leq C_{N}\,|Z|^{-N-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Rem</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>cosh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathrm{Rem}_{N}|\leq\sum_{n=N+1}^{N+2}\frac{|G_{n}|}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{\,n}}+\frac{\cosh\pi}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{N+2}}\,\tau_{N+2}(Z)\\
\leq\frac{C_{N}^{\prime\prime}}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{N+1}}+\frac{C_{N}^{\prime\prime\prime}\,|Z|}{|\operatorname{Im}Z|^{N+2}}\leq C_{N}\,|Z|^{-N-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">using <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}Z|\geq(1+\theta_{0}^{2})^{-1/2}|Z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Im</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}Z|\geq(1+\theta_{0}^{2})^{-1/2}|Z|</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The same argument applies verbatim to
<math id="A1.SS1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\alpha}^{k}F=\sum_{n}\partial_{\alpha}^{k}G_{n}\,e_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\alpha}^{k}F=\sum_{n}\partial_{\alpha}^{k}G_{n}\,e_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> after bounding
<math id="A1.SS1.p6.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\partial_{\alpha}^{k}G_{n}(\alpha)|\leq C(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\partial_{\alpha}^{k}G_{n}(\alpha)|\leq C(n+1)!\,2^{-n/2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>
by the Cauchy formula on the circle <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha^{\prime}-\alpha|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha^{\prime}-\alpha|=1</annotation></semantics></math> applied to
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>; alternatively, apply Cauchy’s formula directly
to the remainder <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Rem}_{N}(\alpha;Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Rem</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Rem}_{N}(\alpha;Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is analytic in <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">(iii) <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is even in <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (each <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>),
so <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\alpha}F(0;Z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\alpha}F(0;Z)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and, by (<a href="#A1.E101" title="In A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">101</span></a>),
<math id="A1.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\tfrac{1}{2}\partial_{\alpha}^{2}F(0;Z)/F(0;Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\tfrac{1}{2}\partial_{\alpha}^{2}F(0;Z)/F(0;Z)</annotation></semantics></math>. By (ii),
<math id="A1.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(0;Z)=1+O(|Z|^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(0;Z)=1+O(|Z|^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so for
<math id="A1.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> large <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F(0;Z)|\geq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F(0;Z)|\geq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the quotient of the two uniform
expansions is again a uniform expansion, whose coefficients are, by
Corollary <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem4" title="Corollary 7.4. ‣ Branch convention. ‣ 7.1. The Appell 𝐹_3 specialization on the physical curve ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a>, exactly <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The cone <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Re}Z|\leq\theta_{0}|\operatorname{Im}Z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Re}Z|\leq\theta_{0}|\operatorname{Im}Z|</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be widened by the termwise estimate above: for
directions closer to the real axis the individual terms <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{n}e_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{n}e_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\asymp|Z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\asymp|Z|</annotation></semantics></math> grow exponentially and the series converges only through
cancellation. The applications of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem27" title="Lemma 7.27. ‣ 7.6. The asymptotic matching: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.27</span></a> in this paper
do not require a wider aperture: the matching of
Subsection <a href="#A1.SS6" title="A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a> is performed along a single vertical
line, the decay statements of Subsection <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5. The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice constant ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> concern
vertical strips, and the coefficients of a Poincaré expansion along
one ray are unique. The mirror symmetry used repeatedly below is the
Schwarz reflection <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}</annotation></semantics></math>, valid because all four
blocks <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{0},\mathsf{K}_{0},\mathsf{S}_{2},\mathsf{K}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{0},\mathsf{K}_{0},\mathsf{S}_{2},\mathsf{K}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are real on
the real axis.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2. </span>Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Uniformly on every closed subsector of
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\arg(\pm is)|&lt;\pi/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\arg(\pm is)|&lt;\pi/2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. off the real axis, and in particular on
every vertical strip <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Re}s|\leq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Re}s|\leq h</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}(s)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm rat}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm rat}(s)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the convergent
trigamma blocks of (</span><a href="#S7.E80" title="In Proposition 7.28. ‣ 7.6. The asymptotic matching: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">80</span></a><span id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) are asymptotic to their
(Bernoulli) Stirling series, with remainders
</span><math id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{N}(|s|^{-N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{N}(|s|^{-N})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> after </span><math id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> terms, and
</span><math id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\psi^{\prime}(s)|+|Q_{\rm rat}(s)|\leq C/|\operatorname{Im}s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\psi^{\prime}(s)|+|Q_{\rm rat}(s)|\leq C/|\operatorname{Im}s|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}=\pm i+O(e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}=\pm i+O(e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
for </span><math id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\to\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\to\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, uniformly in
</span><math id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and likewise
</span><math id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}=\mp i+O(e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∓</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}=\mp i+O(e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
</span><math id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sec^{2}\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sec^{2}\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\csc^{2}(\pi s)=O(e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>csc</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\csc^{2}(\pi s)=O(e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of (</span><a href="#S7.E53" title="In Lemma 7.15. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a><span id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) is
asymptotic to its Poincaré series (</span><a href="#S7.E55" title="In Lemma 7.15. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a><span id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) uniformly on
</span><math id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\arg s|\leq\pi-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\arg s|\leq\pi-\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, for every </span><math id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">(i) and (iii) are Stirling’s formula with remainder in sectors
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, §5.11]</cite> applied to the explicit Gamma quotients; the decay
bound in (i) follows from <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}(z)=O(1/|z|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}(z)=O(1/|z|)</annotation></semantics></math> on
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}z|\geq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}z|\geq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> together with
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}(z+1)=\psi^{\prime}(z)-z^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}(z+1)=\psi^{\prime}(z)-z^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> to reach the arguments <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-s)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-s)/2</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-s/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-s/2</annotation></semantics></math>. (ii) is elementary:
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}\mp i=\mp 2i\,e^{\pm i\pi s}/(1+e^{\pm i\pi s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>∓</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">∓</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}\mp i=\mp 2i\,e^{\pm i\pi s}/(1+e^{\pm i\pi s})</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|e^{\pm i\pi s}|=e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|e^{\pm i\pi s}|=e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|}</annotation></semantics></math> in the indicated
half-planes.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> be (<a href="#S7.E56" title="In Proposition 7.16. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>). Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">there is </span><math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with
</span><math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\varsigma)|\leq C\,|\varsigma|^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\varsigma)|\leq C\,|\varsigma|^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> uniformly on
</span><math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}\varsigma|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}\varsigma|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><em id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph">including</em><span id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
</span><math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}\varsigma\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}\varsigma\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for every </span><math id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> there is </span><math id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{M}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that, uniformly on
</span><math id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}\varsigma\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}\varsigma\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\varsigma)-\sum_{j=2}^{M}\varphi_{j}\,\varsigma^{-j}\Bigr|\leq C_{M}\bigl(|\varsigma|^{-M-1}+|\varsigma|^{-2}e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}\varsigma}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ς</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\varsigma)-\sum_{j=2}^{M}\varphi_{j}\,\varsigma^{-j}\Bigr|\leq C_{M}\bigl(|\varsigma|^{-M-1}+|\varsigma|^{-2}e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}\varsigma}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j}\varphi_{j}\varsigma^{-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ς</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j}\varphi_{j}\varsigma^{-j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the formal series
(</span><a href="#S7.E56" title="In Proposition 7.16. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">); the mirror statement holds for
</span><math id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}\varsigma\leq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}\varsigma\leq-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by
</span><math id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\bar{\varsigma})=\overline{\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\varsigma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ς</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\bar{\varsigma})=\overline{\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(\varsigma)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Everything reduces to the Gamma quotient in
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)=\varsigma\,[\Gamma(\varsigma/2)/\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)=\varsigma\,[\Gamma(\varsigma/2)/\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the right regime
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\arg\varsigma|\leq\tfrac{3}{4}\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\arg\varsigma|\leq\tfrac{3}{4}\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, Stirling gives
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Gamma(\varsigma/2)/\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)=(\varsigma/2)^{-1/2}(1+O(1/\varsigma))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\varsigma/2)/\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)=(\varsigma/2)^{-1/2}(1+O(1/\varsigma))</annotation></semantics></math>
uniformly, whence <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)|\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)|\leq C</annotation></semantics></math> and the
Poincaré expansion (<a href="#S7.E55" title="In Lemma 7.15. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) with uniform remainders
(Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>(iii)). On the left regime
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{3}{4}\pi\leq|\arg\varsigma|\leq\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{3}{4}\pi\leq|\arg\varsigma|\leq\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}\varsigma\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}\varsigma\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
apply the two reflection formulas used in the proof of
Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma 7.15. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.15</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(103)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Gamma(\varsigma/2)}{\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)}=\cot\Bigl(\frac{\pi\varsigma}{2}\Bigr)\,\frac{\Gamma\bigl(\frac{1-\varsigma}{2}\bigr)}{\Gamma\bigl(1-\frac{\varsigma}{2}\bigr)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>ς</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Gamma(\varsigma/2)}{\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)}=\cot\Bigl(\frac{\pi\varsigma}{2}\Bigr)\,\frac{\Gamma\bigl(\frac{1-\varsigma}{2}\bigr)}{\Gamma\bigl(1-\frac{\varsigma}{2}\bigr)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">whose right-hand Gamma arguments have real part tending to <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Beta-integral bound, for <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Bigl|\frac{\Gamma(x)}{\Gamma(x+\frac{1}{2})}\Bigr|=\frac{|\mathrm{B}(x,\tfrac{1}{2})|}{\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{2})}\leq\frac{\mathrm{B}(\operatorname{Re}x,\tfrac{1}{2})}{\sqrt{\pi}}\leq C\,(\operatorname{Re}x)^{-1/2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>π</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Re</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|\frac{\Gamma(x)}{\Gamma(x+\frac{1}{2})}\Bigr|=\frac{|\mathrm{B}(x,\tfrac{1}{2})|}{\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{2})}\leq\frac{\mathrm{B}(\operatorname{Re}x,\tfrac{1}{2})}{\sqrt{\pi}}\leq C\,(\operatorname{Re}x)^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\frac{1-\varsigma}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\frac{1-\varsigma}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cot(\pi\varsigma/2)=-i+O(e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}\varsigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cot(\pi\varsigma/2)=-i+O(e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}\varsigma})</annotation></semantics></math>
(Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>(ii)), gives
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)|\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)|\leq C</annotation></semantics></math> on the left regime as well; (i)
follows since
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}=-\tfrac{(2\varsigma-1)}{4\varsigma^{2}(\varsigma-1)}\widehat{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ς</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}=-\tfrac{(2\varsigma-1)}{4\varsigma^{2}(\varsigma-1)}\widehat{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For (ii): on the left regime, (<a href="#A1.E103" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">103</span></a>) squared gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)=-\varsigma\Bigl[\frac{\Gamma\bigl(\frac{1-\varsigma}{2}\bigr)}{\Gamma\bigl(1-\frac{\varsigma}{2}\bigr)}\Bigr]^{2}\bigl(1+O(e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}\varsigma})\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>ς</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(\varsigma)=-\varsigma\Bigl[\frac{\Gamma\bigl(\frac{1-\varsigma}{2}\bigr)}{\Gamma\bigl(1-\frac{\varsigma}{2}\bigr)}\Bigr]^{2}\bigl(1+O(e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}\varsigma})\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">and the squared quotient has a uniform Stirling expansion in
<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ς</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (right half-plane arguments). The resulting Poincaré
series coincides with (<a href="#S7.E55" title="In Lemma 7.15. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>): both are asymptotic
expansions of the same function <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the open
overlap sector <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{3}{4}\pi&lt;|\arg\varsigma|&lt;\pi-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{3}{4}\pi&lt;|\arg\varsigma|&lt;\pi-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (where the cot
correction is exponentially small in <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varsigma|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varsigma|</annotation></semantics></math>), and the coefficients
of a Poincaré expansion on a sector are unique. (Arithmetically the
same coincidence is the parity identity of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem31" title="Lemma 7.31. ‣ 7.7. The arithmetic step: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.31</span></a>.)
Combining the two regimes, with the exponentially small cot correction
retained additively, gives (ii).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is meromorphic on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with:
double zeros at the negative odd integers; a pole of order <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> at
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=0</annotation></semantics></math>, a simple pole at <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=1</annotation></semantics></math>, double poles at the negative
even integers, and no other poles. The principal-part coefficients at
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=-2m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=-2m</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s-1-2k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s)=\sum_{k\geq 0}\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s-1-2k)</annotation></semantics></math> converges
normally on compact sets avoiding <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and defines a meromorphic
function on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with poles contained in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has (at least) double zeros at the negative even integers, at most
double poles at the negative odd integers, and satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.E104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(104)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T(s)|\leq\frac{C}{|\operatorname{Im}s|},\qquad|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq 1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T(s)|\leq\frac{C}{|\operatorname{Im}s|},\qquad|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">uniformly in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}s</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s+2)-T(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s+2)-T(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma((1+\varsigma)/2)^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text"> has double zeros at
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=-1,-3,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=-1,-3,\dots</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\varsigma/2)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\varsigma/2)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has double poles at
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=0,-2,-4,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=0,-2,-4,\dots</annotation></semantics></math>; combining with the elementary factor
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-(2\varsigma-1)/\bigl(4\varsigma^{2}(\varsigma-1)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ς</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>ς</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ς</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(2\varsigma-1)/\bigl(4\varsigma^{2}(\varsigma-1)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> of
(<a href="#S7.E56" title="In Proposition 7.16. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) gives the stated orders (at <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=0</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{r}}\sim 4/(\pi\varsigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ς</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{r}}\sim 4/(\pi\varsigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}\sim-1/(\pi\varsigma^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">∼</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>ς</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}\sim-1/(\pi\varsigma^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>; at <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=1</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(1)=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{r}}(1)=\pi</annotation></semantics></math>). At <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=-2m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=-2m</annotation></semantics></math> the double-pole
coefficient of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-8m\,\Gamma(m+\tfrac{1}{2})^{2}/\bigl(\pi^{2}(m!)^{2}\bigr)=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8m\,\Gamma(m+\tfrac{1}{2})^{2}/\bigl(\pi^{2}(m!)^{2}\bigr)=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> by the
reflection formula, and the elementary factor contributes an extra
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>. The term <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s-1-2k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s-1-2k)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has
poles only at integers: at <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1+2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1+2k</annotation></semantics></math>, at <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=2+2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=2+2k</annotation></semantics></math>, and at the odd
integers <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1+2k-2m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1+2k-2m</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, where it has a double pole with
principal-part coefficients <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>. At a fixed odd integer these
coefficients are therefore summable in <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and away from small discs
around the integers the terms are dominated by
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>(i); this gives normal convergence and
meromorphy, and shows that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has at most double poles at the negative
odd integers. The double zeros of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=-2m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=-2m</annotation></semantics></math> hold
because every term is then evaluated at a negative odd integer, where
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> has a double zero as a function of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
For (<a href="#A1.E104" title="In Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">104</span></a>): with <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s=Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s=Y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Y|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Y|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, all
lattice points <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma_{k}=s-1-2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ς</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma_{k}=s-1-2k</annotation></semantics></math> have <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}\varsigma_{k}|=|Y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ς</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}\varsigma_{k}|=|Y|</annotation></semantics></math>,
so by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>(i),
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|\leq C\sum_{k\geq 0}\bigl(Y^{2}+(\operatorname{Re}s-1-2k)^{2}\bigr)^{-1}\leq C^{\prime}/|Y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|\leq C\sum_{k\geq 0}\bigl(Y^{2}+(\operatorname{Re}s-1-2k)^{2}\bigr)^{-1}\leq C^{\prime}/|Y|</annotation></semantics></math> by comparison with
<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}(Y^{2}+u^{2})^{-1}du=\pi/|Y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}(Y^{2}+u^{2})^{-1}du=\pi/|Y|</annotation></semantics></math>. The difference
equation is immediate from the definition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the coefficients of the formal series
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}=(2\sinh\partial_{s})^{-1}\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}\in s^{-1}\mathbb{Q}[[s^{-1}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sinh</mi><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ℚ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}=(2\sinh\partial_{s})^{-1}\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}\in s^{-1}\mathbb{Q}[[s^{-1}]]</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#S7.E57" title="In Proposition 7.16. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>). For every
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> there are <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\delta,N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\delta,N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> such that,
uniformly on the sector
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\geq\delta|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\geq\delta|s|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|\geq s_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|\geq s_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|T(s)-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\omega_{j}\,s^{-j}\Bigr|\ \leq\ C_{\delta,N}\,|s|^{-N-1}\ +\ C_{\delta}\,\frac{e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}}{\operatorname{Im}s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|T(s)-\sum_{j=1}^{N}\omega_{j}\,s^{-j}\Bigr|\ \leq\ C_{\delta,N}\,|s|^{-N-1}\ +\ C_{\delta}\,\frac{e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}}{\operatorname{Im}s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mirror statement holds on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\leq-\delta|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\leq-\delta|s|</annotation></semantics></math> with
the same (rational) coefficients, by Schwarz reflection.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq N+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq N+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Insert Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>(ii) termwise:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s)=\sum_{j=2}^{M}\varphi_{j}\,\Sigma_{j}(s)+\mathrm{Err}_{1}+\mathrm{Err}_{2},\qquad\Sigma_{j}(s):=\sum_{k\geq 0}(s-1-2k)^{-j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Err</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Err</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s)=\sum_{j=2}^{M}\varphi_{j}\,\Sigma_{j}(s)+\mathrm{Err}_{1}+\mathrm{Err}_{2},\qquad\Sigma_{j}(s):=\sum_{k\geq 0}(s-1-2k)^{-j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">with
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathrm{Err}_{1}|\leq C_{M}\sum_{k\geq 0}|s-1-2k|^{-M-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Err</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathrm{Err}_{1}|\leq C_{M}\sum_{k\geq 0}|s-1-2k|^{-M-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathrm{Err}_{2}|\leq C\,e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}\sum_{k\geq 0}|s-1-2k|^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Err</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathrm{Err}_{2}|\leq C\,e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}\sum_{k\geq 0}|s-1-2k|^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the error sums split at
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq|s|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;|s|</annotation></semantics></math>: the near terms number at most <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|s|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|s|+1</annotation></semantics></math> and each
is at most <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\operatorname{Im}s)^{-M-1}\leq(\delta|s|)^{-M-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\operatorname{Im}s)^{-M-1}\leq(\delta|s|)^{-M-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 2\delta^{-M-1}|s|^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 2\delta^{-M-1}|s|^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>; the far terms are dominated by
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k&gt;|s|}(2k-1-|s|)^{-M-1}\leq C|s|^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k&gt;|s|}(2k-1-|s|)^{-M-1}\leq C|s|^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathrm{Err}_{1}|\leq C_{\delta,M}^{\prime}|s|^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Err</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathrm{Err}_{1}|\leq C_{\delta,M}^{\prime}|s|^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathrm{Err}_{2}|\leq C_{\delta}\,e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}/\operatorname{Im}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Err</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathrm{Err}_{2}|\leq C_{\delta}\,e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}/\operatorname{Im}s</annotation></semantics></math> as
in (<a href="#A1.E104" title="In Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">104</span></a>). Next, with <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(1-s)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(1-s)/2</annotation></semantics></math> (which satisfies
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\arg a|\leq\pi-\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\arg a|\leq\pi-\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\delta^{\prime}(\delta)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\delta^{\prime}(\delta)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, on the sector),</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{j}(s)=(-2)^{-j}\,\zeta(j,a)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{j}(s)=(-2)^{-j}\,\zeta(j,a),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the Hurwitz zeta function has the classical uniform large-<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>
expansion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, §25.11(xii)]</cite></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(j,a)=\frac{a^{1-j}}{j-1}+\frac{a^{-j}}{2}+\sum_{r=1}^{R}\binom{j+2r-2}{2r-1}\frac{\mathcal{B}_{2r}}{2r}\,a^{-j-2r+1}+O_{j,R}\bigl(|a|^{-j-2R-1}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(j,a)=\frac{a^{1-j}}{j-1}+\frac{a^{-j}}{2}+\sum_{r=1}^{R}\binom{j+2r-2}{2r-1}\frac{\mathcal{B}_{2r}}{2r}\,a^{-j-2r+1}+O_{j,R}\bigl(|a|^{-j-2R-1}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">uniformly on <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\arg a|\leq\pi-\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\arg a|\leq\pi-\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting these finitely
many expansions (each truncated at total order <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+1</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>) and
re-expanding <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(1-s)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(1-s)/2</annotation></semantics></math> in powers of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> produces a fixed formal
series <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{T}=\sum_{j}\hat{\omega}_{j}s^{-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{T}=\sum_{j}\hat{\omega}_{j}s^{-j}</annotation></semantics></math>, with no constant term (the
leading contribution of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is of order <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{1-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{1-j}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> starts at <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=2</annotation></semantics></math>), such that
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s)=\sum_{j\leq N}\hat{\omega}_{j}s^{-j}+O_{\delta,N}(|s|^{-N-1})+O_{\delta}(e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}/\operatorname{Im}s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s)=\sum_{j\leq N}\hat{\omega}_{j}s^{-j}+O_{\delta,N}(|s|^{-N-1})+O_{\delta}(e^{-\pi\operatorname{Im}s}/\operatorname{Im}s)</annotation></semantics></math> on the
sector. It remains to identify <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{T}=\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{T}=\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. The
exact difference equation <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s+2)-T(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s+2)-T(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)</annotation></semantics></math>
(Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>), the uniform expansion just proved (applied
at <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s+2</annotation></semantics></math>, both in the sector), and
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>(ii) at <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varsigma=s+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ς</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varsigma=s+1</annotation></semantics></math> force the coefficientwise
identity <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{T}(s+2)-\widehat{T}(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{T}(s+2)-\widehat{T}(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>-series<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s+1)</annotation></semantics></math>; equivalently, in the
shifted variable <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=s+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=s+1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{T}(u+1)-\widehat{T}(u-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{T}(u+1)-\widehat{T}(u-1)</annotation></semantics></math> equals the
series (<a href="#S7.E56" title="In Proposition 7.16. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) at <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. By
Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem12" title="Proposition 7.12. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.12</span></a> the unique solution of this
equation in <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}\mathbb{Q}[[s^{-1}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}\mathbb{Q}[[s^{-1}]]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A1.SS3.p3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{T}=\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{T}=\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\omega}_{j}=\omega_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\omega}_{j}=\omega_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Propositions <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition A.3. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Proposition A.8. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a> and
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> together prove Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem27" title="Lemma 7.27. ‣ 7.6. The asymptotic matching: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.27</span></a>, in
the uniform quantitative form stated there.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4. </span>The two-component relation and vertical decay</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{0}=\mathsf{S}(0;s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{0}=\mathsf{S}(0;s)</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}_{2}=\partial_{\alpha}^{2}\mathsf{S}(\alpha;s)|_{\alpha=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}_{2}=\partial_{\alpha}^{2}\mathsf{S}(\alpha;s)|_{\alpha=0}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 7.9. ‣ 7.2. The boundary split and the transverse quadrature ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.9</span></a>, define the two
boundary components</p>
<table id="A1.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)=-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{4}+\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{2(\mathsf{S}_{0}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{0})},\qquad\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{4}+\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{2(\mathsf{S}_{0}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{0})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)=-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{4}+\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{2(\mathsf{S}_{0}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{0})},\qquad\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{4}+\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{2(\mathsf{S}_{0}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{0})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">meromorphic functions of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}=\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}=\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (the upper boundary determination),
<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}=\overline{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}=\overline{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the real axis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As an identity of meromorphic functions on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(105)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}-i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)+\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}+i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\Bigl(Q(s)-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{2}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}-i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)+\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}+i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\Bigl(Q(s)-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{2}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\mathsf{K}_{2}/\mathsf{K}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\mathsf{K}_{2}/\mathsf{K}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 7.9. ‣ 7.2. The boundary split and the transverse quadrature ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{t}=\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}=\pi\mathsf{K}_{0}/\mathsf{S}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{t}=\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}=\pi\mathsf{K}_{0}/\mathsf{S}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 7.6. ‣ 7.2. The boundary split and the transverse quadrature ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>). From <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+i\mathfrak{t}=i(\mathfrak{t}-i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+i\mathfrak{t}=i(\mathfrak{t}-i)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-i\mathfrak{t}=-i(\mathfrak{t}+i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-i\mathfrak{t}=-i(\mathfrak{t}+i)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathfrak{t}-i}{1+i\mathfrak{t}}=-i,\qquad\frac{\mathfrak{t}+i}{1-i\mathfrak{t}}=i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathfrak{t}-i}{1+i\mathfrak{t}}=-i,\qquad\frac{\mathfrak{t}+i}{1-i\mathfrak{t}}=i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathfrak{t}-i)\,\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{\mathsf{S}_{0}(1+i\mathfrak{t})}+(\mathfrak{t}+i)\,\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{\mathsf{S}_{0}(1-i\mathfrak{t})}=\frac{-i(\mathsf{S}_{2}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2})+i(\mathsf{S}_{2}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2})}{\mathsf{S}_{0}}=\frac{2\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{\mathsf{S}_{0}}=2\mathfrak{t}\,Q," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>𝖲</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathfrak{t}-i)\,\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{\mathsf{S}_{0}(1+i\mathfrak{t})}+(\mathfrak{t}+i)\,\frac{\mathsf{S}_{2}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{\mathsf{S}_{0}(1-i\mathfrak{t})}=\frac{-i(\mathsf{S}_{2}+i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2})+i(\mathsf{S}_{2}-i\pi\mathsf{K}_{2})}{\mathsf{S}_{0}}=\frac{2\pi\mathsf{K}_{2}}{\mathsf{S}_{0}}=2\mathfrak{t}\,Q,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">and adding the <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\psi^{\prime}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\psi^{\prime}/4</annotation></semantics></math> parts, whose coefficients sum to <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\mathfrak{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mathfrak{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
gives (<a href="#A1.E105" title="In Lemma A.9. ‣ A.4. The two-component relation and vertical decay ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">105</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.10</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> there are <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(h)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}_{\min}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}_{\min}(h)</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q(s)|\leq\frac{C(h)}{|\operatorname{Im}s|},\qquad|\operatorname{Re}s|\leq h,\ |\operatorname{Im}s|\geq y^{\prime}_{\min}(h)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q(s)|\leq\frac{C(h)}{|\operatorname{Im}s|},\qquad|\operatorname{Re}s|\leq h,\ |\operatorname{Im}s|\geq y^{\prime}_{\min}(h),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">uniformly on the strip; in particular <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> at both vertical ends of
every strip, uniformly in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}s</annotation></semantics></math> on compact sets.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solve (<a href="#A1.E105" title="In Lemma A.9. ‣ A.4. The two-component relation and vertical decay ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">105</span></a>) for <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{2}+\frac{(\mathfrak{t}-i)\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}+(\mathfrak{t}+i)\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}}{\mathfrak{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔱</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{2}+\frac{(\mathfrak{t}-i)\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}+(\mathfrak{t}+i)\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}}{\mathfrak{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The vertical strip <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Re}s|\leq h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Re}s|\leq h</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq y^{\prime}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq y^{\prime}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> maps under <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=1-2s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=1-2s</annotation></semantics></math> into
<math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> once <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}_{\min}\geq 2(2h+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}_{\min}\geq 2(2h+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least
the threshold of Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition A.3. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, so
Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition A.3. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>(iii) with <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> gives
<math id="A1.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)|\leq C/|Z|\leq C^{\prime}/|\operatorname{Im}s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)|\leq C/|Z|\leq C^{\prime}/|\operatorname{Im}s|</annotation></semantics></math> there;
the same bound holds for <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the
mirror strip. By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>,
<math id="A1.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\psi^{\prime}(s)|\leq C/|\operatorname{Im}s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\psi^{\prime}(s)|\leq C/|\operatorname{Im}s|</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathfrak{t}\mp i|\leq 3e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔱</mi><mo>∓</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathfrak{t}\mp i|\leq 3e^{-\pi|\operatorname{Im}s|}</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\to\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\to\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math> respectively) and
<math id="A1.SS4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathfrak{t}|\geq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathfrak{t}|\geq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. The claim follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5. </span>The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice
constant</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.11</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be meromorphic on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic, with all poles
contained in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, of order at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> at the odd integers and
at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at the even integers, and suppose that
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(s)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(s)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and as
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, uniformly for
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}s\in[0,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}s\in[0,2]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(s)=\frac{w\,n_{1}(w)}{(w+1)^{k_{1}}\,(w-1)^{k_{0}}},\qquad w=e^{i\pi s}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(s)=\frac{w\,n_{1}(w)}{(w+1)^{k_{1}}\,(w-1)^{k_{0}}},\qquad w=e^{i\pi s},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> a polynomial of degree at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}+k_{0}-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}+k_{0}-2</annotation></semantics></math> (and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>
when <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}+k_{0}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}+k_{0}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>). In particular, if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> then
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> then
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathbb{C}\cdot\sec^{2}\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathbb{C}\cdot\sec^{2}\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mapsto w=e^{i\pi s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mapsto w=e^{i\pi s}</annotation></semantics></math> identifies the cylinder
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}/2\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}/2\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>; a <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic meromorphic
function <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is therefore of the form <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(s)=R(e^{i\pi s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(s)=R(e^{i\pi s})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>
meromorphic on <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. The poles of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=-1</annotation></semantics></math>
(odd integers) and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=+1</annotation></semantics></math> (even integers), with the stated orders,
since <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\mp 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∓</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\mp 1</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes to first order in <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> at the corresponding
integers. The end <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> and the
end <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>; the hypothesis says
that <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(w)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(w)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> and as <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (uniform decay on one
period suffices, every <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math> having a preimage with
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}s\in[0,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}s\in[0,2]</annotation></semantics></math>). Hence <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded near <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, these singularities are removable with value <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is
meromorphic on the Riemann sphere, that is, rational, with poles only
at <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math>, of orders at most <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=n_{0}(w)/((w+1)^{k_{1}}(w-1)^{k_{0}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=n_{0}(w)/((w+1)^{k_{1}}(w-1)^{k_{0}})</annotation></semantics></math> with a polynomial <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree at
most <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}+k_{0}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}+k_{0}-1</annotation></semantics></math> (zero at <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> (zero at <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>): hence
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}=w\,n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}=w\,n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg n_{1}\leq k_{1}+k_{0}-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg n_{1}\leq k_{1}+k_{0}-2</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> this is
<math id="A1.SS5.p1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=c\,w/(w+1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=c\,w/(w+1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4w/(w+1)^{2}=\sec^{2}\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4w/(w+1)^{2}=\sec^{2}\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.12</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(s):=Q(s)-Q_{\rm rat}(s)+\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\;T(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(s):=Q(s)-Q_{\rm rat}(s)+\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\;T(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, in the decomposition
(<a href="#S7.E60" title="In Proposition 7.17. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) one has <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{*}(s_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{*}(s_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for every admissible step-two
lattice, real or complex, and (<a href="#S7.E62" title="In Proposition 7.17. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>) holds with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{*}(s_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{*}(s_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is meromorphic with poles in <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A1.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{0}=\Gamma(1+\tfrac{s}{2})/(\Gamma(1+s)\Gamma(1-\tfrac{s}{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{0}=\Gamma(1+\tfrac{s}{2})/(\Gamma(1+s)\Gamma(1-\tfrac{s}{2}))</annotation></semantics></math> is
entire, with zeros exactly at the negative odd integers and the positive
even integers. <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic on
<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}s&lt;\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}s&lt;\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: the defining series converges locally
uniformly there; at a nonpositive integer <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=-m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=-m</annotation></semantics></math> the only singular
inner terms are those with <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=m</annotation></semantics></math>, present exactly for <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq m+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and
there the double zero of <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((s)_{n}/n!)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((s)_{n}/n!)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=-m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=-m</annotation></semantics></math> cancels the double
pole of <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s+m)^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s+m)^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the finitely many terms with <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>
contain no factor <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s+m)^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s+m)^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>. It extends meromorphically to
<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> by the recurrence (<a href="#S7.E46" title="In item (i) ‣ Theorem 7.9. ‣ 7.2. The boundary split and the transverse quadrature ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>), whose coefficients
vanish only at integers. Hence <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\mathsf{K}_{2}/\mathsf{K}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\mathsf{K}_{2}/\mathsf{K}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is
meromorphic with poles in <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>; so are <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm rat}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm rat}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS5.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A1.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic.</em><span id="A1.SS5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> By (<a href="#S7.E47" title="In item (i) ‣ Theorem 7.9. ‣ 7.2. The boundary split and the transverse quadrature ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>) at <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s+1</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s+2)-Q(s)=\mathsf{f}(s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s+2)-Q(s)=\mathsf{f}(s+1)</annotation></semantics></math>; by the trigamma recurrence,
<math id="A1.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm rat}(s+2)-Q_{\rm rat}(s)=\mathsf{f}_{\rm rat}(s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖿</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm rat}(s+2)-Q_{\rm rat}(s)=\mathsf{f}_{\rm rat}(s+1)</annotation></semantics></math>; by
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>,
<math id="A1.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s+2)-T(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s+2)-T(s)=\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)</annotation></semantics></math>; and
<math id="A1.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tan\frac{\pi(s+1)}{2}=-\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan\frac{\pi(s+1)}{2}=-\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A1.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{f}_{\Gamma}(s+1)=-\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖿</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{f}_{\Gamma}(s+1)=-\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)</annotation></semantics></math>
(Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma 7.15. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.15</span></a>). Hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex176" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(s+2)-\mathcal{D}(s)=\mathsf{f}(s+1)-\mathsf{f}_{\rm rat}(s+1)+\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)=\mathsf{f}_{\Gamma}(s+1)+\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖿</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖿</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝖿</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(s+2)-\mathcal{D}(s)=\mathsf{f}(s+1)-\mathsf{f}_{\rm rat}(s+1)+\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)=\mathsf{f}_{\Gamma}(s+1)+\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\widehat{\mathsf{f}}_{\Gamma}(s+1)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pole orders.</em><span id="A1.SS5.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Because <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic, the pole
order on each residue class may be read off at any one representative.
At <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=-2m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=-2m</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{0}(-2m)=(-1)^{m}\binom{2m}{m}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{0}(-2m)=(-1)^{m}\binom{2m}{m}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic there, so <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic;
<math id="A1.SS5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm rat}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm rat}</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic (its trigamma arguments are
<math id="A1.SS5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}+m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}+m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+m</annotation></semantics></math>); and the simple pole of <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is
cancelled by the double zero of <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>). Hence
<math id="A1.SS5.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic on the even class. At <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=-(2m+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=-(2m+1)</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A1.SS5.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has a simple zero and <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic, so <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>
has at most a simple pole; <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm rat}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm rat}</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic; and
<math id="A1.SS5.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has a simple zero, while <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has at most a double
pole. Hence <math id="A1.SS5.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> has at most a simple pole on the odd class.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Decay at the ends.</em><span id="A1.SS5.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> On the strip
<math id="A1.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}s\in[0,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}s\in[0,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq y^{\prime}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>min</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Im}s|\geq y^{\prime}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, there
is a constant <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A1.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q|\leq c/|\operatorname{Im}s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q|\leq c/|\operatorname{Im}s|</annotation></semantics></math> by Corollary <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem10" title="Corollary A.10. ‣ A.4. The two-component relation and vertical decay ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>,
<math id="A1.SS5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q_{\rm rat}|\leq c/|\operatorname{Im}s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q_{\rm rat}|\leq c/|\operatorname{Im}s|</annotation></semantics></math> by
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>(i), and <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|\leq c/|\operatorname{Im}s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|\leq c/|\operatorname{Im}s|</annotation></semantics></math> by
(<a href="#A1.E104" title="In Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">104</span></a>), while <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Hence
<math id="A1.SS5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(s)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(s)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on the strip as
<math id="A1.SS5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\to\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\to\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma A.11. ‣ A.5. The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice constant ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>. On any step-two lattice <math id="A1.SS5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{0}-2k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{0}-2k\}</annotation></semantics></math> avoiding the
poles, comparison with (<a href="#S7.E60" title="In Proposition 7.17. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) gives
<math id="A1.SS5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{*}(s_{0})=\mathcal{D}(s_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{*}(s_{0})=\mathcal{D}(s_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.13</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem17" title="Proposition 7.17. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.17</span></a> the remainder (<a href="#S7.E62" title="In Proposition 7.17. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>)
is
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(s)=\tfrac{1}{2}Q_{\rm rat}(s)-\operatorname{Re}\mathcal{A}-\tfrac{1}{4}\psi^{\prime}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(s)=\tfrac{1}{2}Q_{\rm rat}(s)-\operatorname{Re}\mathcal{A}-\tfrac{1}{4}\psi^{\prime}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, with no lattice term; and the two-component
relation takes the closed form</span></p>
<table id="A1.E106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(106)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}-i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}+\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}+i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}=-\,T(s)+\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\Bigl(Q_{\rm rat}(s)-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{2}\Bigr)=:X(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}-i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}+\Bigl(\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}+i\Bigr)\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}=-\,T(s)+\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}\,\Bigl(Q_{\rm rat}(s)-\frac{\psi^{\prime}(s)}{2}\Bigr)=:X(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Insert <math id="A1.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=Q_{\rm rat}-\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=Q_{\rm rat}-\cot\frac{\pi s}{2}\,T</annotation></semantics></math>
(Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem12" title="Theorem A.12. ‣ A.5. The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice constant ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>) into (<a href="#A1.E105" title="In Lemma A.9. ‣ A.4. The two-component relation and vertical decay ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">105</span></a>) and use
<math id="A1.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tan\cdot\cot=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>cot</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan\cdot\cot=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One more formal lemma is needed. Let
<math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\psi}(s)=s^{-1}+\tfrac{1}{2}s^{-2}+\sum_{k\geq 1}\mathcal{B}_{2k}s^{-2k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\psi}(s)=s^{-1}+\tfrac{1}{2}s^{-2}+\sum_{k\geq 1}\mathcal{B}_{2k}s^{-2k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> denote
the Stirling series of <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.14</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As an identity in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}[[s^{-1}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}[[s^{-1}]]</annotation></semantics></math>, with the left side re-expanded
in powers of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\psi}(1-s)=-S_{\psi}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\psi}(1-s)=-S_{\psi}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Work in the Borel (Watson) picture, in which
<math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n}c_{n}s^{-n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n}c_{n}s^{-n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the kernel <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n}c_{n}t^{n}/n!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n}c_{n}t^{n}/n!</annotation></semantics></math> and a
shift <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mapsto s-a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mapsto s-a</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds, exactly and coefficientwise, to
multiplication of the kernel by <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{at}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{at}</annotation></semantics></math>. The kernel of <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A1.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\psi}(t)=t/(1-e^{-t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\psi}(t)=t/(1-e^{-t})</annotation></semantics></math>. First,
<math id="A1.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\psi}(t)(1-e^{t})=-te^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\psi}(t)(1-e^{t})=-te^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the kernel of <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\sum_{n\geq 1}ns^{-n-1}=-(s-1)^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\sum_{n\geq 1}ns^{-n-1}=-(s-1)^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="A1.E107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(107)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\psi}(s)-S_{\psi}(s-1)=-(s-1)^{-2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\psi}(s)-S_{\psi}(s-1)=-(s-1)^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">coefficientwise. Second, directly from the parity of the
coefficients, <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\psi}(-x)+S_{\psi}(x)=x^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\psi}(-x)+S_{\psi}(x)=x^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this at
<math id="A1.SS6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=s-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=s-1</annotation></semantics></math> and then (<a href="#A1.E107" title="In Proof. ‣ A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">107</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex178" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\psi}(1-s)=-S_{\psi}(s-1)+(s-1)^{-2}=-\bigl[S_{\psi}(s)+(s-1)^{-2}\bigr]+(s-1)^{-2}=-S_{\psi}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\psi}(1-s)=-S_{\psi}(s-1)+(s-1)^{-2}=-\bigl[S_{\psi}(s)+(s-1)^{-2}\bigr]+(s-1)^{-2}=-S_{\psi}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">All expansions below are along the vertical line
<math id="A1.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=-\tfrac{1}{2}+iY" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=-\tfrac{1}{2}+iY</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>; recall that the coefficients of a
Poincaré expansion along a single ray are unique, so establishing
(<a href="#S1.E13" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) there establishes it as an identity of formal
series. The line lies, for <math id="A1.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=1-2s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=1-2s</annotation></semantics></math>, in <math id="A1.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and in the
sector <math id="A1.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}s\leq-\tfrac{1}{2}|s|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}s\leq-\tfrac{1}{2}|s|</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Y|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Y|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition A.3. ‣ A.1. Coefficient bounds and the bilateral sector expansion ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>(iii),</span></p>
<table id="A1.E108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(108)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)=\sum_{n=1}^{N}g_{n}Z^{-n}+O(|Z|^{-N-1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)=\sum_{n=1}^{N}g_{n}Z^{-n}+O(|Z|^{-N-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}=O(|Z|^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\downarrow}(s)=\overline{\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(\bar{s})}=O(|Z|^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math>
lies in the mirror line. By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>(ii),
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}+i=O(e^{-\pi|Y|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}+i=O(e^{-\pi|Y|})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}-i=-2i+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}-i=-2i+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})</annotation></semantics></math>. The right side of
(<a href="#A1.E106" title="In Corollary A.13. ‣ A.5. The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice constant ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">106</span></a>) is <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/|Y|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/|Y|)</annotation></semantics></math> by (<a href="#A1.E104" title="In Lemma A.7. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">104</span></a>) and
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>(i). Hence, solving
(<a href="#A1.E106" title="In Corollary A.13. ‣ A.5. The classification lemma and the vanishing of the lattice constant ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">106</span></a>) for <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(109)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)=\frac{X(s)}{-2i}+O\bigl(e^{-\pi|Y|}\bigr)=\frac{i}{2}X(s)+O\bigl(e^{-\pi|Y|}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\uparrow}(s)=\frac{X(s)}{-2i}+O\bigl(e^{-\pi|Y|}\bigr)=\frac{i}{2}X(s)+O\bigl(e^{-\pi|Y|}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now expand <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. By the mirror statement of
Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Proposition A.8. ‣ A.3. The Gamma forcing and its lattice sum ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a> (with <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>),
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s)=\sum_{j\leq N}\omega_{j}s^{-j}+O(|s|^{-N-1})+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s)=\sum_{j\leq N}\omega_{j}s^{-j}+O(|s|^{-N-1})+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})</annotation></semantics></math>, with
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\omega_{j}s^{-j}=\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\omega_{j}s^{-j}=\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>; by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ A.2. Uniform asymptotics of the closed blocks ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>(i)
and Corollary <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem13" title="Corollary 7.13. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.13</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm rat}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm rat}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are asymptotic to their Stirling series, the former to the
unique formal solution of its central-difference equation; and
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}=-i+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan\frac{\pi s}{2}=-i+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(s)=-\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}(s)-i\Bigl(Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}(s)-\tfrac{1}{2}S_{\psi}(s)\Bigr)+O(|s|^{-N-1})+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi><mi>ser</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(s)=-\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}(s)-i\Bigl(Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}(s)-\tfrac{1}{2}S_{\psi}(s)\Bigr)+O(|s|^{-N-1})+O(e^{-\pi|Y|})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">in the obvious truncated sense, where <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi><mi>ser</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes
the (rational-coefficient) Stirling series of (<a href="#S7.E52" title="In Corollary 7.13. ‣ 7.3. Formal quadratures and the isolation of the oscillation ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>).
Combining with (<a href="#A1.E108" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">108</span></a>)–(<a href="#A1.E109" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">109</span></a>) and equating
coefficients along the line,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(110)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n\geq 1}g_{n}Z^{-n}=\frac{1}{2}\,Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}(s)-\frac{1}{4}\,S_{\psi}(s)-\frac{i}{2}\,\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}(s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi><mi>ser</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n\geq 1}g_{n}Z^{-n}=\frac{1}{2}\,Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}(s)-\frac{1}{4}\,S_{\psi}(s)-\frac{i}{2}\,\widehat{Q}_{\Gamma}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">all three series on the right being re-expanded in <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> through the
exact substitution <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=(1-Z)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=(1-Z)/2</annotation></semantics></math>. The three series have rational
coefficients, so the splitting of (<a href="#A1.E110" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">110</span></a>) into real and
imaginary parts is coefficientwise:
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}g_{n}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\widehat{q}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}g_{n}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\widehat{q}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is
(<a href="#S1.E14" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), and
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum\operatorname{Re}g_{n}Z^{-n}=\tfrac{1}{2}Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}-\tfrac{1}{4}S_{\psi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi><mi>ser</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum\operatorname{Re}g_{n}Z^{-n}=\tfrac{1}{2}Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}-\tfrac{1}{4}S_{\psi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. For the real part,
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}=\tfrac{1}{16}\psi^{\prime}\bigl(\tfrac{Z+1}{4}\bigr)-\tfrac{1}{16}\psi^{\prime}\bigl(\tfrac{Z+3}{4}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>rat</mi><mi>ser</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}Q_{\rm rat}^{\rm ser}=\tfrac{1}{16}\psi^{\prime}\bigl(\tfrac{Z+1}{4}\bigr)-\tfrac{1}{16}\psi^{\prime}\bigl(\tfrac{Z+3}{4}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> as Bernoulli series (the
arguments <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-s)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-s)/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-s/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-s/2</annotation></semantics></math> equal <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z+1)/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z+1)/4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z+3)/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z+3)/4</annotation></semantics></math>), while
Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem14" title="Lemma A.14. ‣ A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a> gives
<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\tfrac{1}{4}S_{\psi}(s)=\tfrac{1}{4}S_{\psi}(1-s)=\tfrac{1}{4}\psi^{\prime}\bigl(\tfrac{Z+1}{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\tfrac{1}{4}S_{\psi}(s)=\tfrac{1}{4}S_{\psi}(1-s)=\tfrac{1}{4}\psi^{\prime}\bigl(\tfrac{Z+1}{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> as Bernoulli series
(<math id="A1.SS6.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-s=(Z+1)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-s=(Z+1)/2</annotation></semantics></math>); so the real part of (<a href="#A1.E110" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.6. Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A The sectorial estimates ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">110</span></a>) is exactly
(<a href="#S7.E79" title="In Theorem 7.26. ‣ 7.6. The asymptotic matching: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>), in agreement with
Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmtheorem26" title="Theorem 7.26. ‣ 7.6. The asymptotic matching: proof of Theorem ‣ 7. Off the diagonal: the transverse variation and the dyadic law ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.26</span></a>. This proves
(<a href="#S1.E13" title="In Theorem 1.6. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The ultraspherical background of the Jacobi phase expansion, in closed form" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
